{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmSlit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmSlit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithm"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_radial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt_radial","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmSlit.lean#L151-L193","doc":"**`d/dt cLiTwoExt (t·y) = −log(1 − y·t)/t`.**\n\nThe radial derivative of the dilogarithm, by the fundamental theorem of calculus\nrather than by differentiating under an integral sign. Reading it through the\nchain rule, `cLiTwoExt'(ty)·y = −log(1−ty)/t`, i.e. `d/dw Li₂(w) = −log(1−w)/w`\nalong the ray through `y`.\n\nHypotheses: `t ∈ (0,1]` and `y` off the cut. The interval `[0,t]` is inside\n`[0,1]`, where `mem_slitPlane_one_sub_mul` keeps the path off the branch cut. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_liTwoKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_liTwoKernel","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmSlit.lean#L143-L149","doc":"The kernel is continuous at every `t ≠ 0` off the cut. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_ofReal_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cLiTwoExt_ofReal_mul","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmSlit.lean#L117-L139","doc":"**The substitution `u = t·z`.**\n\n`cLiTwoExt (t·y) = −∫₀ᵗ log(1 − y·u)/u du` for real `t ≠ 0`. This is the whole\npoint of the file: on the left the parameter sits *inside* the integrand, on the\nright it is a **limit of integration**, where the fundamental theorem of calculus\nreaches it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.liTwoKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.liTwoKernel","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmSlit.lean#L113-L115","doc":"The `cLiTwoExt` integrand as a function of the integration variable alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_log_one_sub_div_of_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.intervalIntegrable_log_one_sub_div_of_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmSlit.lean#L100-L109","doc":"**The integrand is interval-integrable for every `y` off the cut.**\n\nThis is the statement `qou-clx8` asks for: the integral defining `cLiTwoExt`\nconverges on all of `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)`, *regardless of `‖y‖`* — unlike the series. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.mem_slitPlane_one_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.mem_slitPlane_one_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmSlit.lean#L74-L98","doc":"**`1 − y·z` stays in the slit plane for every `y` off the cut `[1,∞)`.**\n\n`y.im ≠ 0 ∨ y.re < 1` *is* `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)`, since the cut is `{y : y.im = 0 ∧ 1 ≤ y.re}`.\n\nOff the real axis the imaginary part does the work — `Im(1 − yz) = −z·(Im y)`,\nwhich is non-zero for `z > 0`, and at `z = 0` the point is `1`. On the real axis\nbelow `1` the real part does it: `Re(1 − yz) = 1 − z·(Re y) ≥ 1 − max(Re y, 0) > 0`\nfor `z ∈ [0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}